    float Ll[1001];
    for( i = 0; i < 1001; i++ )
        Ll[i] = vips_col_L2Lcmc( i / 10.0 );
    for( i = 0; i < 1001; i++ ) {
        int j;
        for( j = 0; j < 1000 && Ll[j] <= i / 10.0; j++ )
            ;
        LI[i] = (j - 1) / 10.0 +
                (i / 10.0 - Ll[j - 1]) / ((Ll[j] - Ll[j - 1]) * 10.0);
    }
}
```

Same pattern! When j reaches 1000, the loop exits, and `Ll[j]` = `Ll[1000]` which is valid (Ll has 1001 elements, indices 0-1000). But if j=0 (Ll[0] > i/10.0), then `Ll[j-1]` = `Ll[-1]` is out of bounds!

